# Normalise line endings in the repository and in every checkout.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows writes CRLF into the working tree when
# core.autocrlf is true, and the release workflow runs on windows-latest with
# exactly that setting. The compiled archive then carries CRLF text files that
# differ from the blobs in the repository, so the published download cannot be
# checked against the source it was built from.
#
# Text is stored and checked out with LF on every platform. The binary types
# below are excluded, so images, assemblies and the compressed catalog are
# never rewritten.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.gif binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
